WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.362
Where are agencies?

2
00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:05.801
Most on this path run a GCC tenant
synchronized from Active Directory,

3
00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:10.468
with some Conditional Access policies
still report-only, permanent role

4
00:00:10.468 --> 00:00:15.288
assignments left from before PIM, and
applications that still hold secrets.

5
00:00:15.288 --> 00:00:18.765
The APIs are the same in GCC High and DoD;

6
00:00:18.765 --> 00:00:22.787
the endpoints differ,
and so do some features.

7
00:00:22.787 --> 00:00:27.460
Microsoft's U S Government feature
table lists Conditional Access, PIM,

8
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:32.686
access reviews, entitlement management
and Lifecycle Workflows as available,

9
00:00:32.686 --> 00:00:37.200
HR-driven provisioning as partial,
and two features as not available.

10
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.038
GCC uses the commercial Entra service,
so the table doesn't apply to it.

11
00:00:42.038 --> 00:00:45.494
One Azure Government difference
matters for the export:

12
00:00:45.494 --> 00:00:49.464
multifactor authentication's
Trusted IPs isn't supported there,

13
00:00:49.464 --> 00:00:53.876
so network-based exceptions live in
Conditional Access named locations.

14
00:00:53.876 --> 00:00:55.900
The interim paths are on the right.
